/A+A/702/A68           HIRES/Keck radial velocity database       (Teklu+, 2025)
================================================================================
An updated catalog of HIRES/Keck radial velocity measurements.
Including Ca II H&K measurements.
    Teklu J.T., Perdelwitz V., Butler R.P., Trifonov T., Vogt S.S., Mukhija D.,
    Tal-Or L.
    <Astron. Astrophys. 702, A68 (2025)>
    =2025A&A...702A..68T        (SIMBAD/NED BibCode)
================================================================================
ADC_Keywords: Stars, double and multiple ; Exoplanets ; Radial velocities
Keywords: techniques: radial velocities - stars: activity -
          stars: chromospheres

Abstract:
    The first HIRES/Keck precision radial velocity (RV) catalog was
    released in 2017, followed by a second release in 2019, incorporating
    corrections for minor but significant systematic errors. We have
    expanded this catalog to March 2023, with 17971 RV measurements for
    1702 stars. Furthermore, we have included the chromospheric emission
    lines CaII H&K indicator (R'HK), which is among the most prominent
    tracers of stellar activity. The manifestation of stellar activity,
    accompanied by minor systematic errors in high-resolution optical
    stellar spectra, could affect exoplanets detected by the RV method. We
    provide R'HK measurements for~40% of the HIRES catalog alongside RVs
    to mitigate these effects. The precision RVs were obtained using an
    iodine gas absorption cell, and relative, chromospheric emissions at
    the CaII H&K lines were derived from the same spectra used for RV
    measurements. The emitted flux was extracted by rectifying the
    observed spectra with PHOENIX synthetic models across six narrow bands
    surrounding the H and K lines, followed by the subtraction of the
    photospheric contribution. The updated catalog may help distinguish
    stellar activity effects from planetary signals in RV time series,
    corroborating previously detected planetary candidates and aiding the
    detection of new ones.

Description:
    The updated HIRES catalog as of March 2023, which includes 17971
    additional spectra for 1702 stars. This update also addresses minor
    systematic errors in RVs and introduces two new stars: TOI 1173 and
    TYC 1243-262-1. Additionally, it includes the chromospheric emission
    lines CaII H&K indicator (R'HK) for 31218 spectra, representing 40%
    of the total 78920 spectra. The availability of R'HK measurements was
    constrained by data quality, with the highest-confidence
    subset-referred to as the "good sample", comprising 1285 stars out of
    the full catalog of 1702 stars. This subset represents the most
    reliable data for analyzing stellar activity and its impact on RV
    measurements.

